{"requirements":[{"id":"managed_service","requirement":"Run a long-running background worker on node1 as a managed service named inventory-worker.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service is enabled and active. Its heartbeat advanced while PID 2763 remained stable; after reboot it started automatically as PID 846, incremented its persisted start count from 1 to 2, and continued advancing its heartbeat.","evidence_ids":["cmd-27d622328661450a","cmd-846b649e66d04426","cmd-0eb3d3a664e54c90"]},{"id":"write_confinement","requirement":"Confine the worker so it writes only inside /var/lib/inventory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final live namespace showed the root filesystem read-only and /var/lib/inventory writable. Worker-executed probes against /etc, /var/tmp, and /root were denied both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-27d622328661450a","cmd-0eb3d3a664e54c90"]},{"id":"no_new_privileges","requirement":"Ensure the worker gains no new privileges.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The live worker ran under a dedicated unprivileged UID/GID with NoNewPrivs=1 and zero permitted, effective, and ambient capabilities, including after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-27d622328661450a","cmd-846b649e66d04426","cmd-0eb3d3a664e54c90"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The initial service implementation in cmd-8424ece772d24e21 entered a restart loop, but it established the executable, unit, enablement, and state-directory approach used by the completed implementation. The script correction in cmd-d9d5b3f834d94c04 and final account/directory/unit correction in cmd-704c512a25704160 directly contributed to the final solution; the temporary successful /var/tmp probe was immediately removed. The mandated reboot in cmd-7f96c8d2c6a649bf was bounded and necessary for restart evidence. Final observations show no failed services, no new listening sockets, no package damage, and no unrelated temporary residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8424ece772d24e21","cmd-d9d5b3f834d94c04","cmd-704c512a25704160","cmd-7f96c8d2c6a649bf","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. The node-restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart service and boot identity were captured, reboot scheduling was acknowledged, the changed boot identity was independently confirmed, and the service, persisted state, heartbeat, confinement, and privilege restrictions recovered afterward.","limitations":["Write confinement was demonstrated through the live mount namespace and representative worker-executed probes, rather than an exhaustive test of every possible pathname.","There is no cluster state to recover because the managed topology contains only the standalone node1; node and service recovery were directly observed."]}
